<div id="app" v-motion-fade><div class="container"><div class="info-container"><img class="profile-img" :src="profileImage" alt="Profile Image"><div class="personal-info"><h1>Chieh-Jui Ho 何捷睿</h1><p>Email: jerry.ho@iss.nthu.edu.tw</p><br><p>Hi! I'm Jerry. Currently, I'm in my first year pursuing a PhD in Service Science at National Tsing Hua University under the guidance of Prof. <a href="https://soumyaray.com/" target="_blank" class="prof-link">Soumya Ray</a>. My research is primarily focused on the <strong>dynamics of human-AI collaboration</strong>, with a special emphasis on leveraging AI for tailored educational experiences. </p><p>Prior to my doctoral studies, I completed my B.A. degree in an interdisciplinary program of Technology and Art. During this time, I had the valuable experience of working in the UbiComp Lab under Prof. <a href="https://nthu-ubicomp-lab.github.io/#/members/cwyou/home" target="_blank" class="prof-link">Chuang-Wen You</a>. Our work there was dedicated to conducting qualitative research aimed at developing VR applications designed to support mental health.</p></div></div><div class="research-skills"> <h2>Methodologies</h2><p>Experiments (Lab & field experiments)</p><p>Psychometric surveys </p><p>Interview</p><p>Online Platform R&D (front/back-end)</p><p>Data Analysis (choice modeling)</p></div><div class="publications"><h2>Publications</h2><h3>Journal Articles</h3><div class="publications-details"><ol><li>You, C. W., Hung, M. W., Hou, C. T., <strong>Ho, C. -J.</strong>, Yuan, C. W., Bi, N., & Huang, M. C. (2023). Trigger or Treat: Using Technology to Facilitate the Perception of Cravings and Corresponding Cues for Achieving Clinical-friendly Drug Psychotherapy. Proceedings of the ACM on Human-Computer Interaction, 7(CSCW1), 1-26.</li></ol></div><h3>Conference Papers</h3><div class="publications-details"><ol><li><strong>Ho, C.-J.</strong>, Hou, C.-T., Hung, M.-W., Yuan, C. W., Bi, N., Huang, M.-C., & You, C. (2021). CravingProbe: A system